 # NeRF++
 
+Also called: Inverted Sphere NeRF, Unbounded NeRF
 
 ## Overview
-NeRF++ generates novel views for unbounded scenes by separating the scene into a foreground (inside a unit sphere) and a background (outside the sphere) using two separate Neural Radiance Field (NeRF) models [S1, S5]. It solves the parameterization failure of standard NeRF, which assumes the entire scene fits within a bounded volume, leading to missing background elements or loss of detail due to limited sampling resolution in large-scale scenes [S1, S5]. It sets itself apart from its parent [Radiance-field optimization](44-radiance-field-optimization.md) by explicitly handling infinite depth via radial inversion [S5].
