 *   **Measured Performance:** NeRF++ enables high-quality novel view synthesis for unbounded scenes, which standard NeRF fails to do without masking or truncation [S1, S5].
 *   **Strengths:** Handles infinite background; no need for manual masking or background removal; maintains view-dependent effects in the background.
-*   **Limitations:** Requires careful tuning of the sphere radius; performance degrades if the scene geometry does not align well with the spherical partition [G].
 *   **When to use:** Unbounded scenes (e.g., outdoor environments, cityscapes) where the background extends to infinity.
 *   **When not to use:** Bounded indoor scenes where standard NeRF suffices; scenes with strong occlusions that cross the sphere boundary in complex ways.
 
 ## Background
-NeRF++ was introduced by Zhang et al. in October 2020 [S1]. It was developed to address the limitations of the original NeRF [S6], which exhibited large computation requirements, difficulty modeling details of objects within a large scene, and vulnerability to variable illumination and transient occluders [S6]. The method was adapted to generate novel views for unbounded scenes by separating the scene using a sphere, with the inside containing foreground objects and the outside containing the background, which was reparameterized with radial inversion [S1]. It is a foundational method for unbounded NeRF variants.
